function vision_recalc contains a bug that leaves mobile light source at
one place when becoming blind.
For example the player has lit a light at position x=5; y=5, becomes
blind moves to x=4; y=5, but the spotlight of the light source will not
move and stay at x=5; y=5;
this can be seen when checking
light_source *ls;
ls->x  and ls->y

This bug has been found while playing the /dev/null/nethack tournament
2008. Where one challenge depends on light sources and even when blind
these lights have to be updated. Caused by not calling on
do_light_sources(), but rather skipping it.

inside of the sourcecode:
in vision.c
at function:
vision_recalc(control)
...
} else if (Blind) {
/* DO NOT FORGET to update the light sources, though we are blind*/
do_light_sources(next_array);
goto skip;


as a patch file:
diff -r nethack-3.4.3/src/vision.c nethack-3.4.3 orig/src/vision.c
566,567d565
< 	/* DO NOT FORGET to update the light sources, though we are blind*/
< 	do_light_sources(next_array);


